    "Question #: 4": {
      "Title": "Exam SnowPro Advanced Administrator topic 1 question 10 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A Snowflake account is configured with SCIM provisioning for user accounts and has bi-directional synchronization for user identities. An Administrator with access to SECURITYADMIN uses the Snowflake UI to create a user by issuing the following commands:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://img.examtopics.com/snowpro-advanced-administrator/image10.png"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The new user named PTORRES successfully logs in, but sees a default role of PUBLIC in the web UI. When attempted, the following command fails: use DEVELOPER_ROLE;"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Why does this command fail?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. The DEVELOPER_ROLE needs to be granted to SYSADMIN before user PTORRES will be able to use the role."
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. The new role can only take effect after USERADMIN has logged out."
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. USERADMIN needs to explicitly grant the DEVELOPER_ROLE to the new USER."
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. The new role will only take effect once the identity provider has synchronized by way of SCIM with the Snowflake account."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": []
      },
      "Explanation": {
        "content": []
      },
      "Vote_count": [
        {
          "voted_answers": "C",
          "vote_count": 1,
          "is_most_voted": false
        }
      ]
    },
